WEBVTT

00:52:58.000 --> 00:53:00.518
often the work in and of itself
is its own reward.

00:53:00.542 --> 00:53:02.018
If it's not, then the impact

00:53:02.042 --> 00:53:04.684
that you have on each
individual person is meaningful.

00:53:04.708 --> 00:53:06.768
And then the hope is
to scale it over time.

00:53:06.792 --> 00:53:09.018
You don't have to
change the world on day one.

00:53:09.042 --> 00:53:10.684
If the passion is more obsessive,

00:53:10.708 --> 00:53:12.768
it feels more like
something you have to do

00:53:12.792 --> 00:53:14.726
as opposed to something you want to do.

00:53:14.750 --> 00:53:17.184
And then I start to worry
that we're in a situation

00:53:17.208 --> 00:53:19.559
where you feel like,
if I don't change the world,

00:53:19.583 --> 00:53:21.184
then my life has had no meaning.

00:53:21.208 --> 00:53:23.268
And I think that's a sad state of affairs.

00:53:23.292 --> 00:53:26.559
EP: Have you ever wanted to do
something different than what you do?

00:53:26.583 --> 00:53:28.851
AG: Always. That's why
I don't have a real job.

00:53:28.875 --> 00:53:32.059
I just study other people's jobs.
I live vicariously through them.